and complex integration. Learners need to recognize and use it before combining this module's ideas in later work. It appears before estimates because that next topic assumes this starting point."}, {"id": "09a833f9-d1b0-44bd-92b5-271fd19155db", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Estimates", "children": [], "description": "Estimates identifies a specific object, distinction, or relationship within contours and complex integration. Learners need to recognize and use it before combining this module's ideas in later work. After parameterization, estimates supplies what is needed to address primitives."}, {"id": "ddb116cb-fe91-48df-b58b-585c5b7178a6", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Primitives", "children": [], "description": "Primitives identifies a specific object, distinction, or relationship within contours and complex integration. Learners need to recognize and use it before combining this module's ideas in later work. As the final topic in this module, primitives carries the completed idea into cauchy theory."}]}, {"id": "462b8eba-0df5-4774-8648-807571b1ffa8", "type": "topic", "title": "Cauchy theory", "description": "This module builds directly on contours and complex integration and develops cauchy theory. It belongs here because its methods and distinctions are prerequisites for zeros and singularities.", "children": [{"id": "584bd7c9-cf92-4521-bd5b-78152617780f", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Theorem", "children": [], "description": "Theorem provides a formal guarantee or inference rule for cauchy theory, allowing later conclusions to be justified rather than inferred from examples alone. It appears before integral formula because that next topic assumes this starting point."}, {"id": "ed06f4c5-0640-4fb5-a7f8-6ef02757ec9f", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Integral formula", "children": [], "description": "Integral formula identifies a specific object, distinction, or relationship within cauchy theory. Learners need to recognize and use it before combining this module's ideas in later work. After theorem, integral formula supplies what is needed to address derivatives."}, {"id": "63c1c9b1-9991-465b-a12c-dca513489aa2", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Derivatives", "children": [], "description": "Derivatives identifies a specific object, distinction, or relationship within cauchy theory. Learners need to recognize and use it before combining this module's ideas in later work. After integral formula, derivatives supplies what is needed to address consequences."}, {"id": "040aa491-dcb7-4433-8826-503f27de6943", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Consequences", "children": [], "description": "Consequences identifies a specific object, distinction, or relationship within cauchy theory. Learners need to recognize and use it before combining this module's ideas in later work. As the final topic in this module, consequences carries the completed idea into zeros and singularities."}]}, {"id": "9202cc42-d029-46dc-942d-64fbf45149d3", "type": "topic", "title": "Zeros and singularities", "description": "This module builds directly on cauchy theory and develops zeros and singularities. It belongs here because its methods and distinctions are prerequisites for laurent series.", "children": [{"id": "15a7d431-52fe-4a11-bc00-33637dce3cfa", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Isolated zeros", "children": [], "description": "Isolated zeros identifies a specific object, distinction, or relationship within zeros and singularities. Learners need to recognize and use it before combining this module's ideas in later work. It appears before identity theorem because that next topic assumes this starting point."}, {"id": "4d8c50ae-16a2-4791-a6e0-85d1ec98d04c", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Identity theorem", "children": [], "description": "Identity theorem provides a formal guarantee or inference rule for zeros and singularities, allowing later conclusions to be justified rather than inferred from examples alone. After isolated zeros, identity theorem supplies what is needed to address removable singularities."}, {"id": "d4451180-fd29-4741-acc8-950f6881d719", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Removable singularities", "children": [], "description": "Removable singularities identifies a specific object, distinction, or relationship within zeros and singularities. Learners need to recognize and use it before combining this module's ideas in later work. After identity theorem, removable singularities supplies what is needed to address poles."}, {"id": "44a66e65-6301-42b6-bc43-2c0e60a5b1e0", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Poles", "children": [], "description": "Poles identifies a specific object, distinction, or relationship within zeros and singularities. Learners need to recognize and use it before combining this module's ideas in later work. As the final topic in this module, poles carries the completed idea into laurent series."}]}, {"id": "3cb51584-1785-44a5-848e-c1141eaad879", "type": "topic", "title": "Laurent series", "description": "This module builds directly on zeros and singularities and develops laurent series. It belongs here because its methods and distinctions are prerequisites for residues.", "children": [{"id": "a565d88e-d4b8-491a-a523-e5c242e15ad4", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Annuli", "children": [], "description": "Annuli identifies a specific object, distinction, or relationship within laurent series. Learners need to recognize and use it before combining this module's ideas in later work. It appears before classification because that next topic assumes this starting point."}, {"id": "44722c9e-4a88-407d-87c3-4068bb3aeaea", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Classification", "children": [], "description": "Classification identifies a specific object, distinction, or relationship within laurent series. Learners need to recognize and use it before combining this module's ideas in later work. After annuli, classification supplies what is needed to address principal parts."}, {"id": "7ad51234-1a2a-4a9b-91e2-9ba637bb0f40", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Principal parts", "children": [], "description": "Principal parts identifies a specific object, distinction, or relationship within laurent series. Learners need to recognize and use it before combining this module's ideas in later work. After classification, principal parts supplies what is needed to address essential singularities."}, {"id": "a563ed55-b9ee-4161-9489-781ab712975a", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Essential singularities", "children": [], "description": "Essential singularities identifies a specific object, distinction, or relationship within laurent series. Learners need to recognize and use it before combining this module's ideas in later work. As the final topic in this module, essential singularities carries the completed idea into residues."}]}, {"id": "d7c9e444-f1f4-4109-93d9-132d79b49faf", "type": "topic", "title": "Residues", "description": "This module builds directly on laurent series and develops residues. It belongs here because its methods and distinctions are prerequisites for applications.", "children": [{"id": "f584a116-e5e1-4704-96e7-c094850d073d", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Residue theorem", "children": [], "description": "Residue theorem provides a formal guarantee or inference rule for residues, allowing later conclusions to be justified rather than inferred from examples alone. It appears before computation methods because that next topic assumes this starting point."}, {"id": "51074c46-5ea3-4615-a80b-688c0c5b2a9b", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Computation methods", "children": [], "description": "Computation methods is an executable part of residues; its correctness, cost, and failure modes recur in later problems and implementations. After residue theorem, computation methods supplies what is needed to address contour selection."}, {"id": "8553a43e-31cf-4745-97a2-5985d241ca3b", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Contour selection", "children": [], "description": "Contour selection identifies a specific object, distinction, or relationship within residues. Learners need to recognize and use it before combining this module's ideas in later work. As the final topic in this module, contour selection carries the completed idea into applications."}]}, {"id": "2c15173d-f92f-47fb-ab58-ce6e8b41a6d5", "type": "topic", "title": "Applications", "description": "This module builds directly on residues and develops applications. It belongs here because its methods and distinctions are prerequisites for argument principle.", "children": [{"id": "0d0c9a38-c62b-4cf8-a097-2d81e6fdf357", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Real integrals", "children": [], "description": "Real integrals identifies a specific object, distinction, or relationship within applications. Learners need to recognize and use it before combining this module's ideas in later work. It appears before principal values because that next topic assumes this starting point."}, {"id": "23d23b76-6749-4bed-95b9-d5bde4e8a045", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Principal values", "children": [], "description": "Principal values identifies a specific object, distinction, or relationship within applications. Learners need to recognize and use it before combining this module's ideas in later work. After real integrals, principal values supplies what is needed to address sums."}, {"id": "11097957-a0c8-4ed3-8087-7d8e397771c3", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Sums", "children": [], "description": "Sums identifies a specific object, distinction, or relationship within applications. Learners need to recognize and use it before combining this module's ideas in later work. After principal values, sums supplies what is needed to address asymptotic evaluation."}, {"id": "9d7b8e81-fbc9-43cd-bc28-5a105b453822", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Asymptotic evaluation", "children": [], "description": "Asymptotic evaluation makes difficult behavior in applications tractable while exposing the assumptions and accuracy limits used by later methods. As the final topic in this module, asymptotic evaluation carries the completed idea into argument principle."}]}, {"id": "1fe9a766-935f-471f-abd2-55c07b5fd301", "type": "topic", "title": "Argument principle", "description": "This module builds directly on applications and develops argument principle. It belongs here because its methods and distinctions are prerequisites for conformal mapping.", "children": [{"id": "05d1e628-df0a-4f6d-b1db-e69c9f7cf4d5", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Rouché’s theorem", "children": [], "description": "Rouché’s theorem provides a formal guarantee or inference rule for argument principle, allowing later conclusions to be justified rather than inferred from examples alone. It appears before counting zeros because that next topic assumes this starting point."}, {"id": "6766beae-1943-4389-a45f-a3ddf7e8bdee", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Counting zeros", "children": [], "description": "Counting zeros identifies a specific object, distinction, or relationship within argument principle. Learners need to recognize and use it before combining this module's ideas in later work. After rouché’s theorem, counting zeros supplies what is needed to address meromorphic functions."}, {"id": "317715b9-cf49-494c-80fc-ad488468c956", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Meromorphic functions", "children": [], "description": "Meromorphic functions identifies a specific object, distinction, or relationship within argument principle. Learners need to recognize and use it before combining this module's ideas in later work. As the final topic in this module, meromorphic functions carries the completed idea into conformal mapping."}]}, {"id": "17bcbd58-e468-4f55-b678-5d806c82dc93", "type": "topic", "title": "Conformal mapping", "description": "This culminating module draws on argument principle and develops conformal mapping. It belongs last because it requires the earlier tools to be selected, combined, and evaluated rather than used one at a time.", "children": [{"id": "4f4ec8d4-a77e-4956-9e43-7236022f4490", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Möbius maps", "children": [], "description": "Möbius maps gives conformal mapping a reusable representation for organizing assumptions, variables, and relationships before analysis begins. It appears before schwarz lemma because that next topic assumes this starting point."}, {"id": "42b82b55-47b6-4600-ba22-c905d51d1928", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Schwarz lemma", "children": [], "description": "Schwarz lemma identifies a specific object, distinction, or relationship within conformal mapping. Learners need to recognize and use it before combining this module's ideas in later work. After möbius maps, schwarz lemma supplies what is needed to address mapping standard domains."}, {"id": "76d6ba29-6dff-4b40-a14e-7b3f1b078125", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Mapping standard domains", "children": [], "description": "Mapping standard domains gives conformal mapping a reusable representation for organizing assumptions, variables, and relationships before analysis begins. After schwarz lemma, mapping standard domains supplies what is needed to address harmonic applications."}, {"id": "0ccd128d-7ba8-4373-8202-013f85d9f60c", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Harmonic applications", "children": [], "description": "Harmonic applications identifies a specific object, distinction, or relationship within conformal mapping. Learners need to recognize and use it before combining this module's ideas in later work. As the final course topic, harmonic applications requires ideas from the complete path to be integrated and transferred."}]}], "dbBacked": true}$cplxanzzjs$::jsonb,
